lessons[1].sections=[["1. The Promise of a Saviour","God’s saving plan did not begin at the Nativity. The lesson begins with humanity’s need for salvation. God created heaven, earth and human beings. Adam and Eve were the first parents. After their sin they were driven out of the Garden of Eden, but God did not abandon humanity. The promise of a Saviour runs through salvation history."],["2. The Prophecies","The lesson recalls important prophecies about the coming Saviour. Genesis 3:15 points to God’s saving promise. Moses spoke of a prophet like himself. Balaam prophesied that a star would come out of Jacob and a ruler would rise from Israel. Isaiah prophesied that a virgin would bear a son called Immanuel. These promises gave hope and were fulfilled in Jesus."],["3. The Annunciation","Mary lived in Nazareth and was engaged to Joseph. Angel Gabriel appeared to Mary and greeted her, “Hail Mary, full of grace. The Lord is with you.” Mary was surprised and afraid. Gabriel told her not to be afraid because God had chosen her. He announced that she would give birth to Jesus, the Son of the Most High and Saviour of the world. Mary asked how this could happen because she was a virgin. Gabriel explained that the Holy Spirit would come upon her. Mary accepted God’s will: “Here am I, the servant of the Lord.” Jesus took human form in Mary's womb."],["4. The Nativity","Emperor Augustus ordered a census, so Joseph travelled with Mary from Nazareth to Bethlehem. Bethlehem was the city of David. Jesus was born there. Because there was no place for them in the inn, Mary laid the child in a manger."],["5. The Shepherds","Shepherds were keeping watch over their flock at night. An angel announced good news of great joy: a Saviour, the Messiah and Lord had been born in the city of David. A heavenly host praised God. The shepherds went quickly to Bethlehem, saw Jesus and then glorified and praised God."],["6. The Wise Men","Wise men came from the East and followed the star. They came looking for the newborn King. They encountered King Herod and continued towards Bethlehem. The star led them to Jesus. They knelt, paid Him homage and offered gold, frankincense and myrrh."],["7. The Church Seasons","The Annunciation–Nativity seasons help the Church remember God's saving plan and the events surrounding Jesus’ incarnation, birth and childhood. Annunciation Season is the first liturgical season and lasts four weeks. In Syriac it is called Subara, meaning announcement or declaration. The Nativity Season follows it. The lesson also explains B.C., A.D. and Anno Domini and the preparation and abstinence associated with these seasons."]];lessons[1].terms=[["Subara","Announcement or declaration"],["Annunciation","The announcement of Jesus’ birth to Mary"],["Nativity","The birth of Jesus"],["Immanuel","The name in Isaiah’s prophecy concerning the promised child"],["Messiah","The promised/anointed Saviour"],["B.C.","The period before Christ"],["A.D.","The period after Christ in the textbook’s presentation"],["Anno Domini","Year of the Lord"]];lessons[1].facts=[["Mary","The angel of the Lord appeared to ___.","Who did Angel Gabriel visit at the Annunciation?","Mary","Angel Gabriel appeared to Mary at the Annunciation."],["Nazareth","Mary lived in the town of ___.","Where did Mary live?","Nazareth","Mary lived in Nazareth."],["Joseph","Mary was engaged to ___.","To whom was Mary engaged?","Joseph","Mary was engaged to Joseph."],["Gabriel","The angel who appeared to Mary was ___.","Who appeared to Mary?","Gabriel","The angel who appeared to Mary was Gabriel."],["grace","Gabriel greeted Mary, “Hail Mary, full of ___.”","Complete Gabriel’s greeting to Mary.","Grace","Gabriel greeted Mary, “Hail Mary, full of grace.”"],["Mary","The angel said, “Do not be afraid, ___.”","Whom did Gabriel tell not to be afraid?","Mary","Gabriel told Mary not to be afraid."],["Jesus","Mary would give birth to a son named ___.","What was Mary’s son to be called?","Jesus","Mary would give birth to Jesus."],["Most High","Jesus would be called the Son of the ___.","Complete: Son of the ___.","Most High","Jesus would be called the Son of the Most High."],["Holy Spirit","The ___ would come upon Mary.","Who would come upon Mary?","Holy Spirit","The Holy Spirit would come upon Mary."],["Lord","Mary said, “Here am I, the servant of the ___.”","Complete Mary’s response.","Lord","Mary accepted God’s will as the servant of the Lord."],["womb","Jesus took human form in Mary’s ___.","Where did Jesus take human form?","Womb","Jesus took human form in Mary’s womb."],["human beings","God created heaven, earth and ___.","What did God create besides heaven and earth?","Human beings","God created heaven, earth and human beings."],["Adam and Eve","The first parents were ___ and ___.","Who were the first parents?","Adam and Eve","The first parents were Adam and Eve."],["Eden","Adam and Eve were driven out of the Garden of ___.","Which garden did Adam and Eve leave?","Eden","Adam and Eve were driven out of the Garden of Eden."],["Saviour","God promised to send a ___.","What did God promise after humanity’s fall?","Saviour","God promised to send a Saviour."],["Moses","___ said God would raise up a prophet like him.","Which Old Testament figure gave this prophecy?","Moses","Moses spoke of God raising up a prophet like him."],["star","Balaam said a ___ would rise from Israel.","What did Balaam say would rise from Israel?","Star","Balaam prophesied that a star would come out of Jacob."],["Isaiah","___ prophesied that a virgin would bear a son called Immanuel.","Which prophet spoke of Immanuel?","Isaiah","Isaiah prophesied that a virgin would bear a son called Immanuel."],["Augustus","Emperor ___ ordered the census.","Who ordered the census?","Augustus","Emperor Augustus ordered the census."],["Bethlehem","Mary and Joseph went to ___.","Where did Mary and Joseph travel?","Bethlehem","Mary and Joseph travelled to Bethlehem because of the census."],["David","Bethlehem was the city of ___.","Whose city was Bethlehem?","David","Bethlehem was the city of David."],["manger","Mary laid Jesus in a ___.","Where was Jesus laid?","Manger","Mary laid Jesus in a manger because there was no place in the inn."],["shepherds","The first visitors mentioned in the Nativity story were the ___.","Who heard the angelic announcement first?","Shepherds","The shepherds were the first visitors mentioned in the Nativity story."],["Messiah","The angel announced a Saviour, the ___ and Lord.","What title did the angel use for the promised Saviour?","Messiah","The angel announced a Saviour, the Messiah and Lord."],["Bethlehem","The angel said the Saviour was born in the city of ___.","In which city was the Saviour born?","Bethlehem","The angel announced that the Saviour was born in Bethlehem, the city of David."],["gold","The wise men offered Jesus ___.","Name the first gift of the wise men.","Gold","The wise men offered gold."],["frankincense","The wise men also offered ___.","Name the second gift of the wise men.","Frankincense","The wise men offered frankincense."],["myrrh","The third gift was ___.","Name the third gift of the wise men.","Myrrh","The wise men offered myrrh."],["East","The wise men came from the ___.","From which direction did the wise men come?","East","The wise men came from the East."],["Herod","The wise men encountered King ___.","Which king did the wise men encounter?","Herod","The wise men encountered King Herod."],["worship","The wise men knelt and paid Jesus ___.","What did the wise men do when they found Jesus?","Homage","The wise men knelt, paid Jesus homage and offered their gifts."],["B.C.","___ refers to the period before Christ.","What abbreviation refers to the period before Christ?","B.C.","B.C. refers to the period before Christ."],["A.D.","___ refers to the period after Christ in the textbook’s presentation.","What abbreviation is used for the period after Christ?","A.D.","A.D. refers to the period after Christ in the textbook’s presentation."],["Anno Domini","A.D. is associated with the Latin phrase ___.","What Latin phrase is associated with A.D.?","Anno Domini","Anno Domini means Year of the Lord."],["Annunciation Season","The first liturgical season is the ___.","What is the first liturgical season?","Annunciation Season","The Annunciation Season is the first liturgical season."],["four weeks","Annunciation Season lasts ___.","How long does Annunciation Season last?","Four weeks","Annunciation Season lasts four weeks."],["Subara","In Syriac, Annunciation Season is called ___.","What is Annunciation Season called in Syriac?","Subara","In Syriac, Annunciation Season is called Subara."],["Nativity Season","The season following Annunciation Season is the ___.","What season follows Annunciation Season?","Nativity Season","Nativity Season follows Annunciation Season."],["Jesus","The prime event of the Annunciation–Nativity seasons is the birth/incarnation of ___.","What is the prime event remembered in these seasons?","Jesus","The prime event is the birth/incarnation of Jesus Christ, the Saviour."],["welcome","During Annunciation–Nativity we should ___ Jesus as our Saviour and Lord.","What attitude should we have towards Jesus?","Welcome","We should welcome Jesus as our Saviour and Lord and prepare our hearts for Him."]];

lessons[2].sections=[["1. John prepares the way","John the Baptist was the son of Zechariah and Elizabeth and a relative of Mary. He was sent by God to prepare people to receive Jesus. He preached repentance and baptized people in the River Jordan."],["2. Jesus is baptized","Jesus, although without sin, came to John to be baptized and fulfil God’s plan. When Jesus came out of the water, the heavens opened. The Holy Spirit descended like a dove and the Father’s voice declared Jesus to be His beloved Son."],["3. John reveals Jesus","John pointed people towards Jesus and called Him the Lamb of God who takes away the sin of the world. John witnessed that Jesus is the Son of God."],["4. Trinity, Christ and Deneha","The baptism reveals the Holy Trinity: Father, Son and Holy Spirit. Christ means “the anointed.” Deneha is the Feast of Epiphany, celebrated on January 6, and means sunrise or revelation. Jesus is the Light of the World, and John teaches us to introduce Jesus to others."]];lessons[2].terms=[["Christ","The anointed"],["Deneha","Sunrise or revelation; the Feast of Epiphany"],["Holy Trinity","One God in three Persons: Father, Son and Holy Spirit"],["Lamb of God","Jesus, who takes away the sin of the world"],["Light of the World","Jesus, who leads people from darkness towards God’s truth and life"]];lessons[2].facts=[["John","___ the Baptist was the son of Zechariah and Elizabeth.","Who was John the Baptist?","John","John the Baptist was the son of Zechariah and Elizabeth and was sent to prepare people for Jesus."],["relative","John was a ___ of Mary.","What family relationship did John have with Mary?","Relative","John was a relative of Mary."],["repentance","John preached ___.","What did John preach?","Repentance","John preached repentance."],["Jordan","John baptized in the River ___.","Where did John baptize?","Jordan","John baptized people in the River Jordan."],["Jesus","___ came to John to be baptized.","Who came to John for baptism?","Jesus","Jesus came to John to be baptized."],["sinless","Jesus was without ___.","What was Jesus without?","Sin","Jesus was without sin."],["plan","Jesus accepted baptism to fulfil God’s ___.","Why did Jesus accept baptism?","Plan","Jesus accepted baptism to fulfil God’s plan."],["heavens","When Jesus came up from the water, the ___ opened.","What opened at Jesus’ baptism?","Heavens","The heavens opened when Jesus came up from the water."],["dove","The Holy Spirit descended like a ___.","In what form did the Holy Spirit descend?","Dove","The Holy Spirit descended like a dove."],["Father","The ___ spoke from heaven.","Who spoke from heaven?","Father","The Father spoke from heaven."],["beloved","The Father declared Jesus to be His ___ Son.","How did the Father describe Jesus?","Beloved","The Father declared Jesus to be His beloved Son."],["Lamb of God","John called Jesus the ___.","What title did John give Jesus?","Lamb of God","John called Jesus the Lamb of God who takes away the sin of the world."],["Son of God","John witnessed that Jesus is the ___.","Who did John witness Jesus to be?","Son of God","John witnessed that Jesus is the Son of God."],["anointed","Christ means the ___.","What does Christ mean?","Anointed","Christ means the anointed."],["Holy Trinity","The Father, Son and Holy Spirit together are the ___.","What is the Christian name for Father, Son and Holy Spirit?","Holy Trinity","The Holy Trinity is one God in three Persons: Father, Son and Holy Spirit."],["January 6","Deneha is celebrated on ___.","When is Deneha celebrated?","January 6","Deneha is celebrated on January 6."],["Epiphany","Deneha is the Feast of ___.","What feast is Deneha?","Epiphany","Deneha is the Feast of Epiphany."],["sunrise","Deneha means ___ or revelation.","What does Deneha mean?","Sunrise","Deneha means sunrise or revelation."],["Light","Jesus is the ___ of the World.","What is Jesus called in John 8:12?","Light","Jesus is the Light of the World."],["witness","Like John, we should ___ to Jesus and introduce Him to others.","What should we do like John?","Witness","Like John, we should witness to Jesus and introduce Him to others."]];

lessons[3].sections=[["1. Forty days in the wilderness","Before beginning His public life, Jesus went into the wilderness and fasted and prayed for forty days and forty nights. He became hungry, and Satan came to tempt Him."],["2. First temptation — bread","Satan tempted Jesus to turn stones into bread. Jesus answered with God’s Word: we do not live by bread alone, but by every word that comes from God."],["3. Second temptation — test God","Satan tempted Jesus to throw Himself down from the temple and test God. Jesus refused and answered from Scripture that we must not put the Lord our God to the test."],["4. Third temptation — worldly power","Satan offered Jesus the kingdoms of the world if Jesus would worship him. Jesus rejected Satan and taught that only God must be worshipped and served. Satan left, and angels came to serve Jesus."],["5. What this means for us","Jesus overcame temptation through spiritual strength, fasting, prayer and the Word of God. The lesson connects this with abstinence, self-denial, acts of mercy and living according to God’s Word. Lent is the fourth liturgical season and calls us to repentance and preparation for Easter."]];lessons[3].terms=[["Temptation","A test that can lead a person towards sin"],["Prayer","Conversation with God"],["Lent","The fourth liturgical season, a time of fasting, prayer, repentance and preparation for Easter"],["Pethurtha","The first Sunday of Lent in the textbook"],["Holy Week","The last week of Lent, beginning with Palm Sunday and leading to Easter"]];lessons[3].facts=[["forty days and forty nights","Jesus fasted and prayed for ___.","How long did Jesus fast and pray?","Forty","Jesus fasted and prayed for forty days and forty nights."],["Satan","___ tempted Jesus in the wilderness.","Who tempted Jesus?","Satan","Satan tempted Jesus in the wilderness."],["bread","The first temptation was to turn stones into ___.","What was the first temptation?","Bread","Satan tempted Jesus to turn stones into bread."],["Word of God","Jesus answered the first temptation with the ___.","How did Jesus answer the first temptation?","Word of God","Jesus answered with God’s Word that we do not live by bread alone."],["bread alone","Jesus taught that we do not live by ___.","Complete the teaching from the first temptation.","Bread alone","Jesus taught that we do not live by bread alone, but by every word from God."],["temple","In the second temptation Satan asked Jesus to throw Himself from the ___.","From where was Jesus tempted to throw Himself?","Temple","Satan tempted Jesus to throw Himself down from the temple."],["test","The second temptation asked Jesus to ___ God.","What did Satan ask Jesus to do to God?","Test","Jesus refused to test God."],["kingdoms","Satan offered Jesus the ___ of the world.","What did Satan offer Jesus?","Kingdoms","Satan offered Jesus the kingdoms of the world."],["worship","Satan wanted Jesus to ___ him.","What did Satan demand from Jesus?","Worship","Satan demanded worship, but Jesus rejected him."],["God","Jesus taught that only ___ must be worshipped and served.","Whom must we worship and serve?","God","Jesus taught that only God must be worshipped and served."],["angels","After Satan left, ___ came to serve Jesus.","Who came to serve Jesus?","Angels","After Satan left, angels came to serve Jesus."],["spiritual strength","Jesus defeated temptation through ___.","Through what did Jesus overcome temptation?","Spiritual strength","Jesus overcame temptation through spiritual strength."],["fasting","___ strengthens us spiritually.","Name one practice that strengthens us spiritually.","Fasting","Fasting strengthens us spiritually."],["prayer","___ is conversation with God.","What is prayer?","Prayer","Prayer is conversation with God."],["abstinence","Fasting, ___ and prayer strengthen us spiritually.","Name another practice besides fasting and prayer.","Abstinence","Fasting, abstinence and prayer strengthen us spiritually."],["acts of mercy","Helping the sick and poor are examples of ___.","What are helping the sick and poor called in the lesson?","Acts of mercy","Helping the sick and poor are acts of mercy."],["50 days","The Syro-Malabar tradition remembers a period of abstinence of ___ before Easter.","How many days before Easter are mentioned?","50 days","The lesson mentions 50 days of abstinence before Easter."],["25 days","The tradition also mentions ___ days before Christmas.","How many days before Christmas are mentioned?","25 days","The lesson mentions 25 days of abstinence before Christmas."],["Lent","___ is the fourth season of the liturgical year.","What is the fourth liturgical season?","Lent","Lent is the fourth liturgical season."],["Pethurtha","The first Sunday of Lent is called ___.","What is the first Sunday of Lent called in the textbook?","Pethurtha","The first Sunday of Lent is called Pethurtha in the textbook."],["Palm Sunday","Holy Week begins with ___.","What begins Holy Week?","Palm Sunday","Holy Week begins with Palm Sunday."],["Good Friday","On ___ we remember the passion, crucifixion and death of Jesus.","Which day remembers Jesus’ passion and death?","Good Friday","Good Friday remembers the passion, crucifixion and death of Jesus."]];

lessons[4].sections=[["1. Jesus at Nazareth","At the beginning of His public life Jesus went to the synagogue at Nazareth. He was given the scroll of the prophet Isaiah and read the passage about His mission."],["2. Five aspects of His mission","Jesus proclaimed good news to the poor, liberation to those in bondage, sight to the blind, freedom to the oppressed and the year acceptable to the Lord. He then declared that the Scripture had been fulfilled in their hearing."],["3. Total liberation","Jesus freed people from sin, sickness, spiritual bondage and social evils. He forgave sins and healed the paralytic. He healed physical blindness and challenged spiritual blindness such as ignorance, injustice, exploitation and falsehood."],["4. The Kingdom of God","Jesus proclaimed the Kingdom of God through His words, deeds, miracles and presence. The Kingdom is a community where God is Father and people live as brothers and sisters. Justice, peace, joy, love and sharing belong to this life."],["5. The Church continues the mission","The Church helps establish the values of God's Kingdom on earth through its presence, prayer and works. Matthew, Mark, Luke and John are the four Gospels, the first four books of the New Testament."]];lessons[4].terms=[["Poor in spirit","Those who depend on God’s mercy and providence rather than wealth or material power"],["Kingdom of God","A life/community where God is Father, people live as brothers and sisters, and God’s will is fulfilled"],["Total liberation","Freedom from sin, sickness, spiritual bondage and social evils"],["Gospels","Matthew, Mark, Luke and John, the first four books of the New Testament"]];lessons[4].facts=[["Isaiah","Jesus read from the prophet ___.","Which prophet’s scroll did Jesus read?","Isaiah","Jesus read from the scroll of the prophet Isaiah."],["Nazareth","Jesus read the scroll in the synagogue at ___.","Where did Jesus read Isaiah?","Nazareth","Jesus read Isaiah in the synagogue at Nazareth."],["poor","Jesus proclaimed good news to the ___.","To whom did Jesus proclaim good news?","Poor","Jesus proclaimed good news to the poor."],["bondage","Jesus proclaimed liberation to those in ___.","Who were to receive liberation?","Bondage","Jesus proclaimed liberation to those in bondage."],["blind","Jesus proclaimed sight to the ___.","For whom did Jesus proclaim sight?","Blind","Jesus proclaimed sight to the blind."],["oppressed","Jesus proclaimed freedom to the ___.","For whom did Jesus proclaim freedom?","Oppressed","Jesus proclaimed freedom to the oppressed."],["year acceptable to the Lord","Jesus proclaimed the ___.","What fifth mission aspect did Jesus proclaim?","Year acceptable to the Lord","Jesus proclaimed the year acceptable to the Lord."],["fulfilled","Jesus said the Scripture was ___ in their hearing.","What did Jesus say about the Scripture?","Fulfilled","Jesus said the Scripture was fulfilled in their hearing."],["poor in spirit","Those who depend on God’s mercy are the ___.","Who are the poor in spirit?","Poor in spirit","The poor in spirit depend on God’s mercy and providence rather than wealth or material power."],["paralytic","Jesus forgave sins and healed the ___.","Whom did Jesus heal to show authority over sin and sickness?","Paralytic","Jesus forgave sins and healed the paralytic."],["spiritual blindness","Jesus challenged ___ such as ignorance and falsehood.","What kind of blindness includes ignorance and falsehood?","Spiritual blindness","Jesus challenged spiritual blindness such as ignorance, injustice, exploitation and falsehood."],["justice","The Kingdom of God includes ___.","Name one value of God’s Kingdom.","Justice","Justice is one of the values of God’s Kingdom."],["peace","The Kingdom of God includes justice, ___ and joy.","What value comes between justice and joy?","Peace","The Kingdom of God is associated with justice, peace and joy in the Holy Spirit."],["joy","St Paul describes the Kingdom as justice, peace and ___ in the Holy Spirit.","What third value does St Paul mention?","Joy","St Paul describes the Kingdom as justice, peace and joy in the Holy Spirit."],["Father","In the Kingdom of God, God is ___.","Who is God in the Kingdom?","Father","In the Kingdom of God, God is Father and people live as brothers and sisters."],["brothers and sisters","In God’s Kingdom all people are called to live as ___.","How should people live in the Kingdom?","Brothers and sisters","People in God’s Kingdom are called to live as brothers and sisters."],["words","Jesus revealed the Kingdom through His ___, deeds, miracles and presence.","What did Jesus use to reveal the Kingdom?","Words","Jesus revealed the Kingdom through His words, deeds, miracles and presence."],["Church","The ___ works to establish God’s Kingdom on earth.","Who continues Jesus’ mission?","Church","The Church works to establish the values of God’s Kingdom on earth."],["Matthew, Mark, Luke and John","The four Gospels are ___.","Name the four Gospels.","Matthew, Mark, Luke and John","The four Gospels are Matthew, Mark, Luke and John."],["New Testament","The four Gospels are the first four books of the ___.","The Gospels are the first four books of which part of the Bible?","New Testament","The four Gospels are the first four books of the New Testament."]];

lessons[5].sections=[["1. Cana — water into wine","Jesus and His disciples attended a wedding at Cana in Galilee. The family ran out of wine. Mary told Jesus about the problem and trusted Him. She told the attendants, “Do whatever he tells you.” Jesus changed water into excellent wine. This was the beginning of His signs and revealed His glory."],["2. The storm","Jesus and His disciples crossed the Sea of Galilee. A dangerous storm arose while Jesus slept. He rebuked the wind and sea and said, “Peace! Be still!” The sea became calm. The disciples were filled with awe because even the wind and sea obeyed Him."],["3. Bethzatha","In Jerusalem, Jesus met a man who had been ill for thirty-eight years at the pool of Bethzatha. Jesus told him, “Stand up, take your mat and walk,” and the man was healed."],["4. Lazarus at Bethany","Jesus went to Bethany because Lazarus had died. Jesus told Martha, “I am the resurrection and the life.” At the tomb He prayed to the Father and called, “Lazarus, come out!” Lazarus came out alive."],["5. What the signs mean","These miracles are signs that reveal Jesus’ divine glory and call people to believe in Him and proclaim His glory. The lesson also teaches us to trust Jesus and see God’s providence in both victories and defeats."]];lessons[5].terms=[["Cana","The place where Jesus changed water into wine"],["Bethzatha","The pool where Jesus healed the man who had been ill for thirty-eight years"],["Sign","A miracle that reveals Jesus’ glory and points people towards faith"],["Resurrection","Rising from the dead; Jesus says, “I am the resurrection and the life.”"]];lessons[5].facts=[["Cana","At ___ Jesus changed water into wine.","Where did Jesus change water into wine?","Cana","At Cana in Galilee, Jesus changed water into wine."],["wine","The wedding family ran out of ___.","What ran out at the wedding?","Wine","The family at the wedding ran out of wine."],["Mary","___ told Jesus about the lack of wine.","Who told Jesus about the problem?","Mary","Mary told Jesus that the family had no wine."],["no wine","Mary told Jesus, “They have ___.”","What did Mary tell Jesus?","No wine","Mary told Jesus, “They have no wine.”"],["do whatever he tells you","Mary told the attendants, “___.”","What instruction did Mary give the attendants?","Do whatever he tells you","Mary told the attendants, “Do whatever he tells you.”"],["water","Jesus changed ___ into wine.","What did Jesus change into wine?","Water","Jesus changed water into wine."],["signs","The Cana miracle was the beginning of Jesus’ ___.","What did the Cana miracle begin?","Signs","The Cana miracle was the beginning of Jesus’ signs."],["glory","The signs revealed Jesus’ ___.","What did the Cana sign reveal?","Glory","The signs revealed Jesus’ divine glory."],["Sea of Galilee","Jesus and His disciples crossed the ___.","Which sea did Jesus and His disciples cross?","Sea of Galilee","Jesus and His disciples crossed the Sea of Galilee."],["storm","A great ___ arose on the sea.","What arose while Jesus slept?","Storm","A dangerous storm arose while Jesus slept."],["Peace! Be still!","Jesus said, “___” to the wind and sea.","What did Jesus say to the storm?","Peace! Be still!","Jesus rebuked the wind and sea and said, “Peace! Be still!”"],["awe","The disciples were filled with ___ after the storm became calm.","How did the disciples react?","Awe","The disciples were filled with awe because the wind and sea obeyed Jesus."],["thirty-eight years","The man at Bethzatha had been ill for ___.","How long had the man at Bethzatha been ill?","Thirty-eight years","The man at Bethzatha had been ill for thirty-eight years."],["Bethzatha","The sick man was at the pool of ___.","Where was the sick man?","Bethzatha","The man had been ill for thirty-eight years at the pool of Bethzatha."],["Stand up, take your mat and walk","Jesus told the man, “___.”","What did Jesus tell the man at Bethzatha?","Stand up, take your mat and walk","Jesus told the man to stand up, take his mat and walk."],["Bethany","Jesus went to ___ after Lazarus died.","Where did Jesus go because Lazarus had died?","Bethany","Jesus went to Bethany because Lazarus had died."],["Martha","Jesus told ___, “I am the resurrection and the life.”","To whom did Jesus say, “I am the resurrection and the life”?","Martha","Jesus told Martha, “I am the resurrection and the life.”"],["resurrection","Jesus said, “I am the ___ and the life.”","Complete Jesus’ statement.","Resurrection","Jesus said, “I am the resurrection and the life.”"],["Father","At Lazarus’ tomb Jesus prayed to the ___.","To whom did Jesus pray at the tomb?","Father","Jesus prayed to the Father at Lazarus’ tomb."],["Lazarus","Jesus called ___ out of the tomb.","Whom did Jesus call out of the tomb?","Lazarus","Jesus called Lazarus out of the tomb."],["four days","Lazarus had been in the tomb for ___ in the lesson’s key details.","How long had Lazarus been in the tomb?","Four days","Lazarus had been in the tomb for four days."],["believe","Jesus’ signs call people to ___.","What response do the signs call for?","Believe","Jesus’ signs call people to believe in Him."],["proclaim","We are called to ___ Jesus’ glory.","What should believers do with Jesus’ glory?","Proclaim","We are called to proclaim Jesus’ glory."]];

const id=Number(new URLSearchParams(location.search).get("lesson")||document.body.dataset.lesson||1),lesson=lessons[id]||lessons[1];
